# .cursorrules

## Tech Stack
- React 19 + TypeScript (strict)
- Vite 7 with @tailwindcss/vite plugin
- TailwindCSS v4 with CSS custom properties for theming
- shadcn/ui (new-york variant) with Radix UI primitives
- TanStack Query (React Query) for server state
- Wouter for client-side routing
- Express.js backend with TypeScript (ES modules)
- Drizzle ORM with PostgreSQL (Neon serverless)
- Zod for request validation
- Stripe for payments
- Deployed on Vercel (serverless functions)

## Project Structure
- `client/src/pages/` — Page components (one per route)
- `client/src/components/` — Shared components
- `client/src/components/ui/` — shadcn/ui primitives (DO NOT modify directly)
- `client/src/hooks/` — Custom React hooks
- `client/src/lib/` — Utilities and helpers
- `server/controllers/` — Express Router controllers (one per domain)
- `server/stores/` — Database access layer (domain-specific stores)
- `server/services/` — Business logic (service layer)
- `server/middleware/` — Express middleware
- `server/errors/` — Custom error classes
- `server/utils/` — Server utilities
- `shared/` — Shared types, schema, and constants (used by both client and server)

## Code Style
- Use named exports from controllers (barrel export in `server/controllers/index.ts`)
- Hooks follow `use[Domain]` naming convention
- All API calls use `credentials: "include"` for cookie-based auth
- Use `AppError` class from `server/errors/AppError.ts` for server errors
- Use Zod schemas from `server/utils/validation.ts` for request validation
- Never use `any` — use typed interfaces or `unknown`
- Keep components under 300 lines; extract sub-components when larger
- Use `cva` (class-variance-authority) for component variant styling

## Commands
- `npm run dev` — Start development server
- `npm run build` — Build for production
- `npm run db:push` — Push schema changes to database
- `npx drizzle-kit generate` — Generate migrations

## Important
- We use Drizzle ORM — never suggest Prisma or other ORMs
- We use wouter — never suggest react-router
- We use TanStack Query — never suggest SWR
- shadcn/ui components in `components/ui/` should not be modified directly
- All payments go through Stripe — pricing is defined server-side in `shared/tiers.ts`
- The app uses JWT cookie-based auth, NOT session-based auth